     "heading": {
      "zh-Hant": "利沃夫防衛與投降決定",
      "en": "Defence of Lwów and the decision to capitulate"
     },
     "body": {
      "zh-Hant": "波蘭國家記憶研究院（IPN）的九月戰役文章稱，瓦迪斯瓦夫·朗格納將軍是利沃夫防衛的指揮官，他決定向紅軍而不是向德軍投降。依投降條款，軍官與士兵本可自由前往羅馬尼亞或匈牙利，實際上卻向東行進。文章還說，利沃夫的守軍沒有等到由南方戰線部隊、在索斯恩科夫斯基將軍率領下前來的救援。",
      "en": "An IPN article on September 1939 describes Gen. Władysław Langner as the commander of the defence of Lwów, who decided to capitulate to the Red Army rather than to the Germans. Under the surrender terms the officers and soldiers were to be free to cross into Romania or Hungary, but they marched east instead. The article adds that the defenders of Lwów did not see the relief force led by Gen. Sosnkowski with the southern front."
     },
